  "files": {
   ".merges": "copilot\n",
   "b21792a335f3f90b85b3f4fef52ce0ded6c3c72a81e8acacb0205c4380a5bc34/copilot.yml": "target: copilot\nsurfaces:\n  - id: agent-file-model\n    kind: frontmatter\n    items:\n      - item: model\n        key: model\n        domain:\n          values:\n            - o6-model\n        grounds:\n          - declares: key\n            assumption: fixture\n  - id: copilot-config\n    kind: out-of-band\n    location: >-\n      ~/.copilot/config.json subagents.agents.<name>, carrying the native fields `model`, `effortLevel` (this vocabulary's reasoning item, native spelling) and `contextTier` (a native field this vocabulary admits no item for, recorded here as evidence per spec 0197 R12 rather than as a directable item).\n    items:\n      - item: model\n        grounds:\n          - declares: item\n            citation: >-\n              RR -> GitHub Copilot CLI -> Declaration surface: `SubagentSettingsEntry.model` in the bundled `api.schema.json`.\n      - item: reasoning\n        grounds:\n          - declares: item\n            citation: >-\n              RR -> GitHub Copilot CLI -> Declaration surface: `SubagentSettingsEntry.effortLevel` in the bundled `api.schema.json`, plus `copilot help config`'s prose — the native spelling of this vocabulary's reasoning item.\nofferings:\n  - id: o6-offering\n    rank: 1\n    native-value: o6-model\n    provides:\n      intelligence: medium\n      specialization: general\n    encodes:\n      intelligence: o6-offering\n    supports-reasoning-surface: false\n    grounds:\n      - declares: native-value\n        assumption: fixture\n      - declares: provides.intelligence\n        assumption: fixture\n      - declares: supports-reasoning-surface\n        assumption: fixture\nzero-offerings:\n  ground: >-\n    The model lineup actually served to GitHub Copilot CLI is a property of the deployment rather than of the core layer: a GitHub-routed deployment and a bring-your-own-key deployment reach disjoint sets of models. Naming a model the deployment does not serve reproduces the silent routing failure of github/copilot-cli#4437, adjudicated BUG-PRESENT on run 20260902T153919Z-0aa9 (spec 0197 R41).\n  condition: >-\n    A later delta may declare an offering once either github/copilot-cli#4437 is established fixed, or the offerings are restricted to models the deployment's provider is established to serve — deployment knowledge that reaches a mapping through the organization-level override channel of seam (e) rather than through the core layer (spec 0197 R42). The guidance surface a later delta might add is not read as lifting this condition on its own: the ground here is the unknown lineup, not an absent field, and prose naming an unserved model misdirects an orchestrator exactly as a field does.\n  grounds:\n    - declares: ground\n      citation: >-\n        Probe run 20260902T153919Z-0aa9 of issue #1103, verdict BUG-PRESENT against github/copilot-cli#4437 on GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.82 (spec 0197 R41).\n"
  }
 },
